      "widgets_values": [
        "Repaint the entire picture in image 1 as a Renaissance oil painting with the epic grandeur of the classical paintings of Greek myths, imbued with magic and mystery, using the existing moment as the complete composition. Use thin glazed oil layers, sfumato and dramatic chiaroscuro. A heavenly golden light falls on the bird as if it were a messenger of the gods; luminous clouds and drifting motes of light fill the softened background, with rich, jewel-like colour and the hush of a sacred moment. The result must clearly look hand-made, not like a photograph with a filter.\n\nPreserve the bird exactly: its pose, anatomy, proportions, silhouette and field marks, and the local colour of every body region: head, throat, breast, flanks, back and wings. Do not brighten its feathers, add iridescence or replace it with an idealised bird. Image 2 is a photograph of the same bird: match its head pattern, bill shape and the colour of every body region to image 2, not to any other species. Keep its perch, and its place and size in the frame. The background keeps its colours and broad shapes, repainted in the style.\n\nThe bird is the only creature in the picture. The painting is unsigned, with no text, letters, borders or frames."
      ],
